  "summary": "Japanese rock scene aesthetics of theatrical androgyny: elaborate hair, makeup, costumes and gothic-glam stagecraft.",
  "description": "Inspired by Western glam and shock rock, bands like X Japan, Luna Sea and Malice Mizer built Visual Kei (\"visual style\") into full theatrical identity: towering colored hair, kohl and porcelain makeup, aristocratic gothic costumes and stage personas spanning aristocrat, doll and cyber-vampire. Specialist boutiques (h.NAOTO, Moi-même-Moitié) sell the look; bands like Versailles codified substyles (kote-kei, tanbi-kei, osare-kei). It cross-pollinated Lolita fashion and anime character design.",
